This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-tegra-forecr layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Dependencies
============

  URI: git://git.yoctoproject.org/poky.git
  branch: scarthgap

  URI: https://github.com/OE4T/meta-tegra.git
  branch: scarthgap

Patches
=======

Please submit any patches against the meta-tegra-forecr layer to the maintainer:

Maintainer: forecr Support Team <support@forecr.io>

Table of Contents
=================

  I. Adding the meta-tegra-forecr layer to your build
 II. Misc


I. Adding the meta-tegra-forecr layer to your build
=================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-tegra-forecr'

II. Misc
========

Use the following command to install Yocto dependencies on Ubuntu
$ sudo apt-get install -y gawk wget git-core diffstat unzip texinfo gcc-multilib build-essential chrpath socat libsdl1.2-dev xterm zstd

Create a working directory for Yocto
$ YOCTO_DIR=/home/$USER/yocto-tegra
$ mkdir $YOCTO_DIR

Select the latest stable branch (as of June 2023)
$ export BRANCH="scarthgap"

Download Yocto's Poky base meta-layer 
$ cd $YOCTO_DIR
$ git clone -b ${BRANCH} git://git.yoctoproject.org/poky.git poky

Download meta-tegra (contains L4T 36.3.0 as of June 2024) 
$ git clone -b ${BRANCH} https://github.com/OE4T/meta-tegra.git

Download meta-tegra-forecr
$ git clone -b ${BRANCH} https://github.com/forecr/meta-tegra-forecr.git

Initialize the build environment 
$ source poky/oe-init-build-env build

# Update $YOCTO_DIR/build/conf/local.conf and $YOCTO_DIR/build/conf/bblayers.conf files

Build the image with developer tools such as GStreamer, NVIDIA plugins, etc
$ bitbake core-image-sato-dev
or
$ bitbake core-image-weston
or
$ bitbake core-image-base


